Third-party OAuth client identity
---------------------------------

Codescribe ships public desktop OAuth client ids for two providers so account
sign-in works without the operator pasting a registration. Neither id is a
secret. Settings and env overrides are always checked first.

OpenAI (ChatGPT account / Codex CLI public app id):

    app_EMoamEEZ73f0CkXaXp7hrann

This is the public OAuth client id used by OpenAI's Codex CLI for the ChatGPT
desktop loopback flow (preferred redirect host localhost, path /auth/callback,
preferred port 1455). Codescribe reuses it so "Sign in with ChatGPT" works out
of the box; it does not claim to be the Codex CLI. Override with
LLM_OPENAI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID or CODESCRIBE_OPENAI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID.

xAI (Grok / Grok CLI public client id):

    b1a00492-073a-47ea-816f-4c329264a828

This is the client id xAI publishes for the Grok CLI as a public desktop OAuth
client. Codescribe uses it as the default so xAI sign-in works without the
operator registering an application; it is not a private registration and
Codescribe does not claim to be the Grok CLI. Product sign-in follows OpenCode's
SuperGrok path: RFC 8628 device authorization (open a verification URL, poll
for tokens) — not a local loopback callback on 127.0.0.1:56121. Override with
LLM_XAI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID or CODESCRIBE_XAI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID.

Anthropic account login stays gated on the operator supplying their own
registration (paste-code flow; no shipped default).
